---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { imageWidths } from '@lib/images';
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import fallingCameras from '@assets/images/about/falling-cameras.webp';
import workshop from '@assets/images/about/workshop-laptop.jpg';
import hannahCamera from '@assets/images/about/hannah-with-camera.jpg';
import jumping from '@assets/images/about/jumping-off-sofa.webp';
import signature from '@assets/images/about/signature.png';
import { MQ } from '@config/breakpoints';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Building effective online spaces for creators - Engage with your audience"
  description="Baya Garden Studio aims to help you build an effective digital space that allows you to engage with your audience and automate your business online."
>
  <div class="about">
    <header class="about__intro">
      <h1>A <span class="accent">community</span> and <span class="accent">one stop shop</span> for the creative market pitching their tent in the digital world</h1>
      <p class="about__lede">Baya Garden Studio will help your business become more visible, connect with your tribe and thrive online.</p>
    </header>

    <Image
      src={fallingCameras}
      alt="Hannah taking a self portrait with cameras falling around her"
      layout="full-width"
      widths={imageWidths(fallingCameras)}
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
      class="about__hero"
    />

    <div class="about__band">
    <section aria-labelledby="began">
      <h2 id="began" class="about__began-title">How it all began.</h2>
      <div class="about__story">
      <div class="about__began">
        <p>I’ll never forget the first time I built a website.</p>
        <p>
          Back in 2015, I started an engineering workshop for children and with limited capital to fund the business, I
          decided to build the website myself using Wix. I’ve always been quite creative and a problem solver, so after a
          little research on the internet, I was able to build an online space in one night.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Image src={workshop} alt="A child building a robot at a laptop in the engineering workshop" widths={imageWidths(workshop)} sizes={`${MQ.mdDown} 100vw, 28vw`} class="about__photo about__photo--offset" />
      <Image src={hannahCamera} alt="Hannah smiling and holding a camera with a flash" widths={imageWidths(hannahCamera)} sizes={`${MQ.mdDown} 100vw, 28vw`} class="about__photo" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="about__columns">
      <p>
        It served my business adequately for about a year but then the Wix platform was no longer the best fit for my
        business needs (I will say that Wix has a much better offering today than what was on offer back then). I wanted
        greater flexibility to build my website in the way that I envisioned it and the idea of owning my website and
        having the ability to move it whenever I needed to became important to me which was how I was introduced to
        Wordpress.
      </p>
      <p>
        Over the years, my focus has shifted from building websites for myself to building digital spaces for other
        businesses. Through running two businesses – an engineering children’s workshop and a photography business, I
        learnt the importance of community, building trust and designing systems that allowed a business to thrive.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="about__lean" aria-labelledby="lean">
      <Image src={jumping} alt="A child leaping off a sofa mid-air, in black and white" widths={imageWidths(jumping)} sizes={`${MQ.mdDown} 100vw, 60vw`} />
      <div>
        <h2 id="lean">Lean business is the goal.</h2>
        <p>
          I’m passionate about lean businesses which means I believe that your business should free you from
          overwhelming responsibilities that takes away from what matters to you most. This is why making your website
          work harder for you is central to the Baya Garden Studio approach.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="about__columns">
      <div>
        <p>
          Armed with a comprehensive tech strategy, your space should be optimised to engage with your audience and
          streamline your business processes.
        </p>
        <p>
          I have learned a lot over the years about optimising businesses and I am obsessed about refining my strategies
          and sharing the best tried and true approaches with you so that you don’t have to waste time starting from
          scratch.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          I love sharing best practices here at the Baya Garden Studio. Connect with me through my newsletter to receive
          quick tips on what’s working today.
        </p>
        <Image src={signature} alt="Signed, Hannah Ogunyinka" widths={imageWidths(signature, 416)} sizes="26rem" class="about__signature" />
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about__intro {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 50% 15% 35%;
    row-gap: var(--stack-s);
    padding: var(--space-md);

    @media (--md-down) {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--stack-s);
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    text-transform: capitalize;
  }

  .accent {
    color: var(--color-purple);
  }

  .about__lede {
    grid-column: 3;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);

    @media (--md-down) {
      grid-column: auto;
    }
  }

  .about__hero {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  /* Padding and gaps scale with the page width, as on the live site. */
  .about__band {
    display: flex;
    padding: 6%;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3vw; /* token-exempt: scales with the page, as on the live site */
  }

  .about p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about p + p {
    margin-top: var(--stack-s);
  }

  /* Paragraphs that are columns side by side take no stacking gap. */
  .about__columns > p + p {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
    text-transform: none;
  }

  /* Theme columns 33.38% / 33% / 33.62% with a 3vw gap; WordPress shrinks
     them in proportion, which is what these fr values give. */
  .about__story {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 33.38fr 33fr 33.62fr;
    column-gap: 3vw;
    align-items: start;

    @media (--md-down) {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      row-gap: var(--stack-s);
    }
  }

  .about__began-title {
    margin-bottom: calc(var(--space-lg) * 0.6);
  }

  .about__photo {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 3 / 4;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--radius-panel);
  }

  /* The theme drops the first photo by about 3vw. */
  .about__photo--offset {
    margin-top: 3vw;

    @media (--md-down) {
      margin-top: 0;
    }
  }

  .about__columns {
    display: grid;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--container-about);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-block: var(--space-xl);
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-md);

    @media (--md-down) {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0;
    }
  }

  /* Theme columns 69% / 33% with a 3vw gap, shrunk in proportion. */
  .about__lean {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 69fr 33fr;
    column-gap: 3vw;
    align-items: center;

    @media (--md-down) {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    /* Never stretched past the photo's own 1024px, as on the live site;
       only the text column is centred. */
    :global(img) {
      display: block;
      align-self: start;
      width: 100%;
      max-width: var(--photo-lean-max);
      height: auto;
      aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
      object-fit: cover;
      border-radius: var(--radius-panel);
    }

    /* Theme: the heading's small gap plus a 2vw block gap above the text. */
    h2 {
      margin-bottom: calc(var(--space-sm) + 2vw);
      line-height: var(--leading-heading);
    }
  }

  /* Theme: 407px wide at a 2.96 ratio, contained, one small gap below the text. */
  .about__signature {
    display: block;
    width: min(100%, 25.4rem); /* token-exempt: signature artwork width */
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 2.96; /* token-exempt: theme's signature box */
    object-fit: contain;
    margin: var(--space-sm) auto 0;
  }
</style>
